  "lifecycle_and_result_contract": [
    "The driver runs stages sequentially and does not hold the inner lock. Each actual command holds the same nonblocking exclusive qualification-owner-pin.lock; AISHELL uses that same lock.",
    "Both require a terminal unchanged-source default gate for the supplied new head/tree, and preserve its original nonzero exit. A successful independent stage cannot repair a failed default.",
    "Every opt-in command requires exactly one anchored successful harness summary with its declared passed count, zero failed and zero ignored. Filtered cases are not added to coverage.",
    "An ordinary test failure remains in the batch, while source/script/artifact or compilation failures stop later stages. The whole batch cannot return zero with a failed child stage.",
    "The selected case source hashes remain exact; original model expectations, assertions and deadlines were not edited.",
    "AISHELL binds one normal example compiler-artifact to its exact package, source, profile and target path; runs once with the original WAV and configuration; preserves exact stdout/stderr and original exit, and checks source/config/model/WAV/executable/script before and after.",
    "AISHELL retains build 300 seconds, inference 60 seconds, internal total 560 seconds and caller-owned outer 600 seconds, CPU 200 percent and memory 8 GiB. It records inference admission only after Popen succeeds."
  ],
